Article 3
Paragraph (1) what is meant by "physical violence" is any act that results in pain, injury, wounds or disability to a person's body, miscarriage, fainting and or causes death. What is meant by "psychological violence" is an act that results in fear, loss of self-confidence, loss of ability to act, feelings of helplessness and or severe psychological suffering to a person. What is meant by "sexual violence" is any act in the form of sexual harassment, forced sexual relations, forced sexual relations in an unnatural or unwanted manner, forced sexual relations with others for commercial purposes and or certain purposes. What is meant by "exploitation" includes: acts that exploit a child economically or sexually with the intention of benefiting oneself or others;
acts with or without the consent of the victim that
b.
include but are not limited to prostitution, forced labor or services, slavery or similar practices, oppression, extortion, exploitation of physical, sexual, reproductive organs, or unlawfully removing or transplanting organs and/or body tissues or exploiting the labor or ability of a person by another party to obtain benefits both material and immaterial.
c. all forms of exploitation of sexual organs or other body organs of the victim to obtain benefits, including but not limited to all activities of prostitution or sexual abuse.
What is meant by "trafficking in persons" is the act of recruitment, transportation, harboring, sending, transfer, or receipt of a person by threat of violence, use of violence, abduction, confinement, forgery, fraud, abuse of power or position of vulnerability, debt bondage or giving payment or benefits, so as to obtain consent from the person holding control over that other person, whether conducted within a country or between countries, for the purpose of exploitation or resulting in a person being exploited.
What is meant by "Household Neglect" is: an act that results in the non-fulfillment of a child's needs properly, whether physical, mental, spiritual or social;
b. an act of deliberately neglecting to maintain, care for, or look after a child as appropriate;
c. an act that neglects a person within the scope of their household, whereas according to the law applicable to them or because of an agreement or contract they are obliged to provide life, care, or maintenance to that person;
d. an act that results in economic dependence by means of limiting and/or prohibiting proper work inside or outside the home so that the victim is under the control of that person. What is meant is deviant behavior of children such as the use of glue/aibon that can cause children to feel addicted or intoxicated because they are invited by their friends, and deviation towards free sex behavior or the use of prohibited items.
Paragraph (2) Sufficiently clear.
Paragraph (3) Sufficiently clear.

Article 4
Every woman and child who becomes a victim of physical violence, psychological violence, exploitation or trafficking shall have the right to obtain protection and services.
The protection, assistance, and services for victims as referred to in paragraph (1) include:
a. to be respected for their dignity as human beings;
b. complaints or requests for protection from the person concerned and/or other parties; c. confidential handling or placement of victims in safe locations and houses whose whereabouts are kept secret to avoid intimidation and threats;
medical services/health treatment in the form of
